As suggested in the comments, you can use the ordered keyword to get the output in order. In practice you want to have a lot of independent computations and then only print (or copy or whatever) the result in order. Not an expert on this but here is how I do it (works on gcc and msvc): #include <stdio.h>
#include <omp.h>

int blah(int argc, char* argv[]) {
