434.
4343.43123 How can I avoid such an output?

answers.body:
The reason is the printing is not defined as an atomic operation, thus context switch occurs while printing to the standard output is still ongoing. Solution: You must make the for loop body an atomic operation, using #pragma omp atomic #pragma omp parallel for
for (int i=0; i<1000000; i++) {
    if (test.successful() == true) {
        #pragma omp atomic
        std::cout << test.id() << " " << test.result() << std::endl;
    }
}

