for(int i = 0; i < 10; i++){
    myFunc(i);
} I do not want to send 1, 3, 6 together or 2 4 7 together. Can I manage which numbers are sent together?

answers.body:
You should read about chunk size as maybe it can help you Scheduling examples For example if you will be good with taking 1,2 and 3,4 and 5,6 and so on you can do this simply by this code: #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static, 2) 
for(int i = 0; i < 10; i++){
    myFunc(i);
} This schedule(static, 2) means that each thread will take 2 continues numbers like this: Thread 1 : 1,2 Thread 2 : 3,4 Thread 3 : 5,6 And so on until there is no more data. If you want different scheduling take a look at link at the beginning of the post. But note that some of them may come with some additional overhead.

